---
description: >-
  Regression fixture (per its own source comment): a node declared inside a
  `global` block stays anchored at root level even though a flow container
  immediately references it, instead of being pulled into that container.
---
%% Without the `global` block, referencing A inside the flow would pull it
%% into the container. Declaring it global anchors it at root level.
agentflow-beta TB

global
  A["Shared input"]
end

flow pipeline["Pipeline"]
  A --> B["Process"] --> C["Publish"]
end
